  "title": "Lee et al. 2019 (Motor Imagery) — EEG dataset and OpenBMI toolbox for three BCI paradigms: an investigation into BCI illiteracy",
  "description": "A motor imagery EEG dataset from 54 healthy participants performing binary left/right hand grasping imagery across two sessions on different days. Recordings were made with 62 EEG channels plus 4 EMG channels at 1000 Hz. The data belong to a larger multi-paradigm BCI collection (MI, ERP, SSVEP) used to investigate BCI illiteracy and variation in decoding performance across subjects and sessions.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 1000 Hz with 62 Ag/AgCl electrodes and a BrainAmp amplifier, nose-referenced and grounded at AFz, with impedance kept below 10 kOhm. Participants sat 60 cm from a 21-inch LCD monitor and imagined grasping with the hand indicated by a left or right arrow cue for 4 s. Each session included an offline training phase and an online test phase of 100 trials each, and four EMG channels were recorded alongside the EEG.",
